<title>USA: Meridian Medical Q3 oper income increases.</title>
<headline>Meridian Medical Q3 oper income increases.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBIA, Md. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Condensed Statement of Pre-tax-Income</p>
<p>	    Three and Nine Months Ended April 30</p>
<p>					$000</p>
<p>					     Three Months  Nine Months</p>
<p>						 Proforma	   Proforma</p>
<p>				    Actual  Combined  Actual  Combined</p>
<p>				     1997	1996     1997     1996</p>
<p> Revenues			 10,680   10,315   29,663   25,907</p>
<p> Operating Income		  962	332    1,999	589</p>
<p> Pre-tax Income		    589	210	144	202</p>
<p>NOTE:  Meridian Medical Technologies Inc said its third quarter ended April 30.</p>
<p>The company said its actual and proforma combined results assume Survival Technology Inc and Brunswick Biomedical Corp were fully merged to form Meridian Medical during the specified period and exclude one-time, non-recurring merger related costs of $4,464,000 in for the third quarter of 1996, $3,949,000 in the first nine months of 1997 and $4,464,000 in the first nine months of 1996.</p>
<p>The company said it did not report net income or earnings per share because the numbers would not have been applicable with the merger.</p>
